  "facts": [
    "Opened in 1967, the 6,596‑metre San Bernardino Tunnel became the second‑most vital Swiss freight artery after the Gotthard crossing, linking eastern Switzerland with the Canton of Ticino.",
    "A 1991‑2006 overhaul lowered the centre channel, added an emergency escape tunnel, and upgraded ventilation, turning the original single‑lane bore into a safer, modern passage.",
    "Speed‑check cameras enforce an 80‑km/h limit, and the tunnel’s narrow, single‑lane design forbids overtaking, keeping traffic flow smooth compared to the busier St. Gotthard Tunnel."
